      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-299075",
      ":question/problem": "A circle has center $C$, and points $D$ and $E$ lie on the circle. Line segments $DF^(\u2015)$ and $EF^(\u2015)$ are tangent to the circle at points $D$ and $E$, respectively. If the radius of the circle is $48$ millimeters and the perimeter of quadrilateral $CDFE$ is $206$ millimeters, what is the distance, in millimeters, between points $C$ and $F$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
