      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-299088",
      ":question/problem": "A circle has center $U$, and points $T$ and $V$ lie on the circle. Line segments $TW^(\u2015)$ and $VW^(\u2015)$ are tangent to the circle at points $T$ and $V$, respectively. If the radius of the circle is $36$ kilometers and the perimeter of quadrilateral $UTWV$ is $226$ kilometers, what is the distance, in kilometers, between points $U$ and $W$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
